# What EAS Build must NOT upload.
#
# `mobile/` lives inside the website's repo, and there are no npm workspaces joining them — so when
# EAS archives the project it walks up to the git root and takes the whole thing. The first attempt
# uploaded 664 MB, almost none of which the app build can use.
#
# .easignore replaces .gitignore entirely for the archive, so this file has to re-state the things
# .gitignore already excludes (node_modules, .next) as well as the web-only content.

node_modules/
.next/
.git/

# The website's own code and assets. The app talks to it over HTTPS and needs none of it at build
# time; public/ alone is 391 MB of store and product photography.
public/
app/
components/
drizzle/
docs/
scripts/
data/
extension/
types/
_to_delete/
*.patch

# Local env and build leftovers
.env*
.vercel/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
